The single V3 reviewer run completed with exit code 0 in the fixed WSL repository. It used reviewer SHA-256 `cf8e0e71983b7212bc0394d2ea74ae2e7ea7d44710c4013d03442040767646cf`, V5 collector SHA-256 `eca35da46e0054b182b4e9a4b105ec5d70fc794b8ae2f8d092efc0d6adb7dc5e`, intake SHA-256 `b9ed0177266af986b72e7c8457e00fe3a40f21aa2cb974c96ad31ee381d3f7ea`, proposal SHA-256 `6f008480d40dc46880a8dda195168d50788f499466992ff7dece901b0b84d670`, and accepted-baseline SHA-256 `7277981c004f0712e34d34e08f5d0ef4b070df2e1a05eae2dd8a01a9761e91ca`.

The reviewer V3 changes only the proposal status expected by V2 to the exact V5 value, `SOURCEONLY_RECORD_APPEND_PROPOSAL_REQUIRES_SEPARATE_TERMINAL_VERIFICATION`. Before this run, the actual proposal keys and the intake/census/records wrapper schema were read and checked; its intake, baseline, collector, and artifact refs matched the supplied hashes. The earlier V2 attempt and its BLOCKED stdout are preserved separately.

The actual stdout is preserved at `source-reviews/20261024d-after226-independent-terminal-review-V3-actual.stdout.json`, SHA-256 `2283943cfa2974e0d323ff03734bd232d47b9a197742efb9439856c3706acd8c`. It reports:

- 229 owned modules, 6,310 complete records, 6,291 distinct full names, and 161 unique owned-receipt paths.
- 91 new records: 41 for `Part4ActualThirdOriginalClosedSplitAggregation`, 41 for `Part4ActualThirdOriginalFirstChordQuery`, and 9 for `Part3FreeEpsilonActualCount`.
- Old census entries and all 6,219 old records deeply equal; current source and present object slots rehashed for all 229 owned modules.
- Three original strict producers PASS; one original audit group with one ALL stage and three stock replays.
- Result scope: finite owned modules and explicitly bound direct suppliers under normal imported-environment trust. No full project/import/external closure replay, no unconditional main theorem, no proof credit, and no ROOT acceptance.

This reviewer calls the statically peer-reviewed V5 `propose()` in memory and compares its result with the actual proposal. Its producer gates are shared with V5, not a second independent implementation of every guard. No Lean, LeanChecker, compiler, audit, CI, or acceptance/census/records write occurred during the reviewer run. `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` was set for V5's read-only provider checks.
